            <div xml:id="d660">

                <pb facs="0850" n="762" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv02/pg762"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">663.119/orig: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Sharp</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Acting Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-12-17T16:00:00+00:00"
                            >December 17, 1918—4 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 5:16 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6340. War Trade Board [from Taylor]: No. 692, attention White. We have made no
                    agreement that consignments to Adriatic ports should depend on War Trade Board
                    receiving import authorization from Inter-Allied Bureau and no such organization
                    exists at present. War Trade Board must not sign away liberty of action.
                    Taylor.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sharp</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
